                "name": "Ideas that engineer or manage a beneficial microbiome or biofilm on textiles",
                "description": "Solutions that focus on establishing, sustaining, evolving, or modulating a community of microorganisms (a microbiome or biofilm, potentially multi-species, self-regenerating, temporary, or controllably detachable/sheddable/dispersible) directly on or within the textile to provide continuous hygiene, odor control, or self-cleaning properties. This includes in-situ production/release of agents, transformation of soils, physical contaminant trapping (including via EPS), preemptive niche occupation, mimicking inter-microbial competition, or emulating natural purification systems like Schmutzdecke. These systems may require specific care/maintenance or be designed for biodegradability post-use, and can involve direct surface colonization, cultivation on/in fibers, or surface display of enzymes.",
