                        "mode_of_action": "1. Dormant microbial spores are integrated into the fabric during manufacturing. 2. The user activates the fabric with a light mist of water or body humidity. 3. Spores germinate into active microbes. 4. The microbes produce and secrete enzymes or biosurfactants that degrade organic soil and odor molecules. 5. The fabric is refreshed, and the microbes return to a dormant state as it dries.",
