                        "idea_summary": "This concept delivers the cleaning power of microbes without the microbes themselves. An 'a-cellular' spray contains a cocktail of potent enzymes or biosolvents, harvested from engineered microorganisms, to offer immediate, high-potency stain removal in a familiar, shelf-stable format.",
                        "core_principle": "Utilizing purified, high-concentration enzymes, biosolvents, or enzyme-laden nanovesicles derived from engineered microbes for rapid, targeted stain degradation without the use of live organisms.",
                        "form_factor": "An aerosol or pump spray containing a stabilized, cell-free solution of biocatalysts (e.g., lipases, proteases) or biological nanostructures like Outer Membrane Vesicles (OMVs).",
                        "mode_of_action": "1. User sprays the solution directly onto a stain. 2. The concentrated enzymes or nanovesicles immediately begin to catalytically break down the target molecules (e.g., fats, proteins). 3. The reaction is fast and efficient, requiring no incubation time. 4. The broken-down residue can be blotted away with a damp cloth.",
