                        "mode_of_action": "1. The garment is made with fibers containing or coated with photosynthetic microbes. 2. During wear, the microbes are largely dormant in darkness. 3. Exposing the garment to light (e.g., hanging it in a window) provides the energy for the microbes to actively break down accumulated sweat and soil. 4. The process is passive and requires no water.",
