                        "idea_summary": "A preventative solution where fabrics are treated with a mycelium-derived coating that repels water-based stains and actively inhibits the growth of odor-causing microbes. This approach focuses on keeping clothes cleaner for longer, thereby extending the time between necessary washes.",
                        "core_principle": "A thin, biocompatible coating derived from mycelium provides a dual-action protective barrier that is both hydrophobic and antimicrobial.",
                        "form_factor": "An invisible, breathable coating applied to the surface of finished textiles.",
                        "mode_of_action": "1. A liquid solution containing mycelial biopolymers is applied to fabric as a final finish. 2. The solution cures to form a durable, micro-porous layer. 3. The layer's hydrophobic properties repel liquids, while its inherent antimicrobial compounds prevent bacterial colonization.",
