                        "optimized_idea": "Core-Shell Fibers with Encapsulated Bio-Agents for Controlled Release",
                        "idea_summary": "Fibers are engineered with a protective outer shell and a core loaded with dormant microbes, spores, or stabilized enzymes. This structure shields the bio-agents during manufacturing and wear. Release is triggered by specific conditions like moisture, pH change, or mechanical stress, delivering the cleaning function precisely when and where it's needed.",
                        "core_principle": "Micro-encapsulation within a core-shell fiber structure, where an inert outer sheath protects a core of active biological agents from environmental degradation until release is triggered.",
