                        "mode_of_action": "1. Core-shell fibers containing encapsulated bio-agents are woven into a garment. 2. The outer shell protects the agents from UV light, high temperatures, and harsh chemicals. 3. A trigger (e.g., the moisture and pH change from sweat) makes the shell permeable or causes it to rupture. 4. The cleaning agents are released from the core directly onto the fabric surface to act on soils.",
