                    "group_name": "Catalytic Fiber Platforms",
                    "group_summary": "This group focuses on engineering the fabric itself as a high-performance catalytic surface, using either immobilized biological agents (enzymes) or synthetic catalysts (photocatalytic nanoparticles). The goal is to create durable, reusable cleaning functionality that is an inherent property of the material.",
                    "descriptive_title": "Advanced Catalytic Materials for Water-Free Fabric Decontamination",
                    "one_liner_summary": "This portfolio of ideas transforms fabric into an active catalytic platform by grafting enzymes, embedding light-activated nanoparticles, or using controlled-release fibers.",
