                    "group_name": "Bio-Integrated Textiles",
                    "group_summary": "This theme focuses on embedding biological cleaning functions directly into the fabric's structure. These solutions aim to create self-cleaning or continuously refreshing garments by integrating engineered fibers, layered microbial zones, or sensor-activated systems.",
                    "descriptive_title": "Functionalized Textiles for In-Situ Biological Cleaning",
                    "one_liner_summary": "Embedding engineered fibers, microbial layers, and sensor systems directly into textiles to enable continuous or on-demand cleaning.",
