                        "idea_summary": "Specific, high-efficiency enzymes are permanently grafted onto fabric fibers, turning the garment into a catalytic surface that continuously digests stains and soils. Activated by minimal moisture, this approach provides targeted, biological-level cleaning without the complexity of maintaining a living system.",
                        "core_principle": "Utilizes stabilized, non-living enzymes that are immobilized or grafted onto textile fibers to catalytically break down specific types of organic soils (e.g., proteins, lipids, starches) with minimal moisture.",
