                        "mode_of_action": "1. Stabilized enzymes (e.g., lipases, proteases) are chemically bonded to the fabric. 2. When a stain occurs, minimal moisture activates the immobilized enzymes. 3. The enzymes specifically break down the target soil molecules into smaller, soluble parts. 4. The residue can be easily wiped or rinsed away with very little water.",
