                        "idea_summary": "Textiles are engineered with integrated molecular traps, such as activated carbon or cyclodextrins, that actively adsorb odor molecules and volatile organic compounds from sweat. This approach keeps the garment feeling fresh for much longer, extending wear time and significantly reducing the need for washing to control odor.",
                        "core_principle": "Leverages adsorbent materials like Granular Activated Carbon (GAC) or cyclodextrins integrated into the fabric to trap and neutralize odor molecules and organic contaminants.",
