                    "uuid": "00231b5b-4b88-4be9-9c44-93387239a3e8",
                    "group_name": "Living & Bio-Integrated Textiles",
                    "group_summary": "This theme explores textiles that function as living ecosystems, either by being made from biological materials like mycelium or by hosting beneficial microbial communities. These approaches aim for continuous, self-sustaining hygiene by leveraging biological processes to metabolize waste and outcompete pathogens.",
                    "descriptive_title": "Bio-Integrated Materials for Continuous Self-Cleaning Textiles",
                    "one_liner_summary": "A portfolio of concepts that integrate living organisms (microbes, fungi) into or as the fabric itself to create a self-sustaining, cleaning ecosystem.",
                    "selling_point": "This approach moves beyond passive materials to create \"living\" garments that actively maintain their own hygiene, promising a paradigm shift in clothing care and longevity.",
