                        "mode_of_action": "1. Dormant, encapsulated spores remain inert on the dry fabric. 2. The garment is exposed to a trigger (e.g., misting with water, sweat). 3. The capsules rupture or become permeable, releasing nutrients and hydrating the spores. 4. Spores germinate into active bacteria, which produce and secrete enzymes/surfactants to break down local soil. 5. As the fabric dries, the bacteria form new, dormant spores, ready for the next cycle.",
