                        "optimized_idea": "Biomimetic Anti-Fouling Textiles for Contaminant Repellency",
                        "idea_summary": "Textiles are engineered with micro- or nano-scale surface textures that mimic natural anti-fouling surfaces like lotus leaves (superhydrophobicity) or shark skin (low drag). This structure prevents dirt, liquids, and microbes from adhering firmly, allowing them to be shed easily with minimal mechanical action or water.",
