                    "group_name": "Mechano-Physical Interventions",
                    "group_summary": "This theme focuses on using physical forces and micro-scale structures, rather than chemistry or biology, to maintain hygiene. These concepts either kill microbes on contact through mechanical rupture or use physical forces like static electricity to manage particulate soil.",
                    "descriptive_title": "Bio-Inspired Nanotextures and Physical Forces for Non-Chemical Hygiene",
                    "one_liner_summary": "A collection of ideas that use engineered surface topographies to physically destroy bacteria or electrostatic forces to capture and release dirt.",
