                        "optimized_idea": "Microfluidic-Integrated Garments for Targeted, Low-Water Cleaning",
                        "idea_summary": "This concept enables ultra-low-water spot cleaning by building a precision fluid delivery system into the garment itself. Instead of immersing the entire piece of clothing, micro-channels or zoned materials can transport and apply a few drops of cleaning solution directly to a stain, which is then wicked away, achieving effective cleaning with minimal resource use.",
                        "core_principle": "Integrates microfluidic channels or zoned material properties directly into a garment to enable the precise, automated delivery of minute amounts of water or cleaning solution to specific areas.",
                        "form_factor": "A garment constructed with hollow capillary-action fibers or with distinct zones of varying material properties (e.g., wicking, antimicrobial).",
                        "mode_of_action": "1. A garment is constructed with different functional zones (e.g., high-odor areas are antimicrobial, high-stain areas have microfluidic channels). 2. When a specific area needs cleaning, a tiny amount of cleaning fluid is introduced at an input port. 3. Capillary action draws the fluid through integrated micro-channels directly to the soiled spot. 4. The fluid dissolves the stain and is then wicked away to an evaporative zone, leaving the area clean and nearly dry.",
