                        "idea_summary": "A fabric coated with semiconductor nanoparticles that, when exposed to ambient or UV light, generate reactive oxygen species to decompose organic soil, stains, and odor-causing microbes. This offers an active, water-free method to 'recharge' the cleanliness of a garment.",
                        "core_principle": "Generation of highly reactive oxygen species (ROS) via photocatalysis on a semiconductor-coated surface when exposed to light photons.",
                        "form_factor": "A permanent coating of photocatalytic nanoparticles (e.g., TiO2, ZnO) grafted onto textile fibers. Can be used in garments or in accessories like wardrobe liners or sanitizing bags.",
                        "mode_of_action": "1. The garment is exposed to a light source (sunlight or artificial). 2. Nanoparticles on the fabric absorb photons, creating electron-hole pairs. 3. These react with water vapor and oxygen in the air to produce ROS. 4. These potent oxidizers break down organic molecules (dirt, bacteria) into harmless components.",
