                        "optimized_idea": "Textiles with Embedded Antimicrobial Nanomaterials for Passive Sanitization",
                        "idea_summary": "This solution provides continuous, passive hygiene by embedding antimicrobial agents directly into the fabric, which inhibit the growth of odor-causing bacteria and other microbes. Unlike mechanical methods, this approach uses material chemistry to maintain sanitation, thereby reducing the need for frequent washing.",
                        "core_principle": "Incorporates non-leaching nanomaterials (e.g., silver ions, quaternary ammonium compounds, functionalized carbon) that disrupt microbial metabolism or cell integrity.",
