                    "name": "Ideas that achieve hygiene via non-chemical, physical antimicrobial mechanisms",
                    "description": "Solutions that provide antimicrobial effects on textiles without relying on chemical agents, for instance, by using material surface topographies (e.g., biomimetic, nano-scale, piercing) that physically damage, lyse, or detach microorganisms, or via contact-killing surfaces that may require debris removal.",
                    "parent_uuid": "160aa0b6-52e2-4503-ab7d-742e873b3df8",
