                        "idea_summary": "A textile that functions as a reusable catalyst, continuously breaking down organic soils like sweat and oils with minimal moisture. Unlike washing with detergents, this approach embeds the cleaning agent directly and durably into the fabric for a persistent, low-water self-cleaning effect.",
                        "core_principle": "Immobilizes robust, stabilized enzymes by covalently bonding them to textile fibers, creating a surface with persistent catalytic activity against specific types of soil.",
