                        "mode_of_action": "1. The garment is exposed to a light source (e.g., sunlight, an LED). 2. The photocatalytic particles on the fibers become energized. 3. They react with water vapor and oxygen in the air to create hydroxyl radicals and superoxide. 4. These radicals attack and break down dirt and microbes into harmless volatile compounds.",
