                        "core_principle": "The use of high-aspect-ratio nanostructures integrated into fabric to induce lethal mechanical stress on microbial cell membranes upon contact.",
                        "form_factor": "Standard textile fabric where the sanitizing mechanism is inherent to the fiber's surface structure.",
                        "mode_of_action": "1. Bacteria comes into contact with the nanostructured fiber surface. 2. The sharp nanopillars or nanoneedles physically pierce the bacterial cell wall. 3. The cell ruptures, leading to death without the use of chemicals or water.",
