                        "idea_summary": "A smart fabric coating that changes its surface properties in response to a simple trigger (e.g., pH change, light, mild heat), causing it to release adhered dirt and microbes. This allows for rapid, low-water 'refresh' cleaning by simply rinsing or brushing away the released contaminants.",
                        "core_principle": "Using stimuli-responsive polymers that can switch between a contaminant-adhering state and a contaminant-repelling state.",
                        "form_factor": "A thin polymer coating applied to conventional textiles.",
