                        "idea_summary": "A specialized cleaning system that uses supercritical carbon dioxide (scCO2) as a non-aqueous solvent to sanitize and clean clothes. This technology offers a complete replacement for water, leveraging the unique solvating properties of scCO2 to remove oils and kill microbes without fabric damage.",
                        "core_principle": "Exploits the dual gas-like and liquid-like properties of carbon dioxide above its critical point to dissolve and remove contaminants and sterilize textiles without water.",
                        "form_factor": "A high-pressure, closed-loop chamber system capable of managing the temperature and pressure required to achieve and maintain supercritical CO2.",
                        "mode_of_action": "1. Clothes are placed in a high-pressure vessel. 2. The vessel is filled with liquid CO2 and pressurized/heated past its critical point (31°C, 1070 psi). 3. The scCO2 permeates the fabric, dissolving oils and inactivating microbes. 4. The pressure is released, CO2 returns to a gas and is recycled, leaving clothes clean and dry.",
