                        "optimized_idea": "Sonic and Air-Pulse System for Mechanical Biofilm Dislodging",
                        "idea_summary": "A cleaning device that uses focused sonic waves and high-pressure air pulses, combined with a minimal amount of water or cleaning mist, to physically blast biofilms and dirt from fabric. This approach mimics industrial cleaning techniques to maximize physical removal forces while minimizing water consumption.",
                        "core_principle": "Applies intense, localized mechanical energy (cavitation from sonics, shear force from air pulses) to overcome the adhesion forces of biofilms.",
