                        "optimized_idea": "Superhydrophobic Fabric with 'Roll-Off' Mist Cleaning",
                        "idea_summary": "A self-cleaning fabric that uses a physical mechanism, inspired by the Lotus leaf, to shed dirt and contaminants with just a light misting of water. This approach prevents dirt from adhering in the first place and uses the mechanical action of rolling water droplets for cleaning, requiring no chemical detergents.",
                        "core_principle": "Leverages a textile surface with extreme water-repellency (superhydrophobicity), causing water droplets from a mist to maintain a high contact angle, picking up and carrying away dirt particles as they roll off.",
                        "form_factor": "A textile with a nano-structured surface treatment. Cleaning is performed with a standard water mister.",
