                        "idea_summary": "This concept uses microfluidics—the science of manipulating tiny volumes of liquid—to create a hyper-efficient spot-cleaning tool. By delivering a precise, picoliter-scale dose of cleaner directly into the fabric's weave, it can remove a stain using an almost imperceptible amount of fluid, representing the ultimate in cleaning precision and water conservation.",
                        "core_principle": "Microfluidic channels precisely control the flow and delivery of a minute quantity of potent cleaning fluid, applying it directly to the stained area with minimal waste or overspray.",
