                        "idea_summary": "This 'Air Wash' concept uses energized gas (plasma or ozone) to clean clothes without any water or physical contact. It effectively 'burns off' odors and surface contaminants at a molecular level, providing a powerful method for deodorizing and sanitizing garments between wears.",
                        "core_principle": "A sealed chamber generates atmospheric plasma or concentrated ozone gas to create reactive species that oxidize and neutralize organic soils, odors, and microbes on fabric surfaces.",
                        "form_factor": "A closet, cabinet, or bag-like appliance that uses electricity to generate a cleaning gas, requiring no water or chemical inputs.",
                        "mode_of_action": "1. Clothes are hung inside the appliance. 2. An electrical discharge generates plasma or ozone from the surrounding air. 3. The reactive gas species permeate the fabric, oxidizing volatile organic compounds (odors) and killing microbes. 4. A ventilation or decomposition cycle removes any remaining ozone, leaving the clothes refreshed.",
