                        "mode_of_action": "1. A soiled area is identified. 2. The microfluidic device or patch is placed over the stain. 3. A minimal, precise volume of a concentrated cleaning fluid (e.g., enzymes, solvents) is dispensed through the micro-channels directly into the stain. 4. The concentrated agent breaks down the stain locally, which can then be blotted away. 5. The surrounding fabric remains completely dry.",
