                        "optimized_idea": "Fungal Bioreactor for Decolorizing and Recycling Laundry Water",
                        "idea_summary": "A compact bioreactor that uses immobilized fungal cultures (mycelium) to specifically target and break down complex organic molecules like dyes and detergents in laundry water. This allows for the continuous reuse of water while preventing color transfer and chemical buildup.",
                        "core_principle": "Leverages the unique enzymatic capabilities of fungi (e.g., laccases, peroxidases) to decolorize and degrade persistent organic pollutants in wastewater.",
                        "form_factor": "A cartridge containing a porous substrate with immobilized fungal cultures, designed to be integrated into a laundry appliance's water loop.",
                        "mode_of_action": "1. Laundry water is passed through the fungal bioreactor cartridge. 2. Fungal enzymes break down dyes and detergent residues. 3. The purified, decolorized water is returned to the system for reuse.",
