                        "optimized_idea": "Garment Cleaning via Advanced Oxidation Process (AOP) Atomizer",
                        "idea_summary": "A compact device that generates a fine mist containing powerful but short-lived oxidative species (like hydroxyl radicals) to chemically break down contaminants directly on the fabric. This method uses minimal water as a carrier and leverages advanced chemistry for purification, offering an alternative to biological or surfactant-based cleaning.",
                        "core_principle": "In-situ generation of highly reactive oxygen species (AOP) to chemically oxidize organic soils, using water primarily as a delivery medium rather than a solvent.",
                        "form_factor": "A handheld device or a compact chamber that integrates an AOP generator (e.g., UV/H2O2, ozone) and an atomizer.",
