                    "group_summary": "This theme explores completely waterless cleaning methods that rely on energy input—in the form of light or electricity—to generate potent sanitizing agents like reactive gas, plasma, or photocatalytic radicals within a contained device.",
                    "descriptive_title": "Energy-Driven Systems for Waterless Garment Sanitization",
                    "one_liner_summary": "A collection of water-free sanitization chambers and bags that use light or electricity to activate chemical and physical cleaning processes.",
