                        "idea_summary": "This concept proposes a 'Nespresso machine for detergent,' where a small appliance synthesizes a fresh, potent, and customized cleaning solution from stable, shelf-stable cartridges on-demand. This approach minimizes packaging, transport emissions, and waste, while delivering a highly effective, low-volume cleaning agent.",
                        "core_principle": "Cell-free synthetic biology is used to produce concentrated cleaning agents (e.g., enzymes, surfactants) on-demand and at the point of use, eliminating the need for shipping water-based products and reducing waste.",
                        "form_factor": "A compact, countertop appliance containing cartridges of freeze-dried biological reagents (DNA, cell extracts). It takes in a small amount of water and power to synthesize a dose of cleaning solution.",
                        "mode_of_action": "1. A reagent cartridge is inserted into the device. 2. The user selects the type of cleaning agent needed. 3. The device rehydrates the reagents and initiates a cell-free synthesis reaction. 4. After a short period, a small, concentrated dose of the cleaning agent is dispensed.",
