                        "mode_of_action": "1. Soiled laundry water enters the bioreactor tank for biological treatment. 2. The water is then drawn through a fine-pore membrane via suction. 3. The membrane physically blocks bacteria and suspended solids, while allowing clean water to pass through for reuse. 4. The biological process continues to clean the water remaining in the tank.",
