                        "optimized_idea": "Electrostatic Garment for Waterless Particulate and Pathogen Removal",
                        "idea_summary": "This garment utilizes fibers that maintain a persistent electrostatic charge to attract and bind airborne particulates, dust, and microbes. Cleaning is achieved without water by simply neutralizing the charge, which releases the trapped contaminants for easy removal by shaking or brushing.",
                        "core_principle": "Employs electrostatic adhesion to physically bind and remove particulate contaminants from a garment's surface without using water.",
                        "form_factor": "A textile made from electret fibers or materials that can be easily charged.",
                        "mode_of_action": "1. The garment fibers are electrostatically charged. 2. During wear, oppositely charged particles (dust, pollen, microbes) are attracted to and bound to the fibers. 3. To clean, the charge is neutralized (e.g., via a conductive wipe or exposure to an ion stream). 4. The adhesion force is eliminated, and the trapped particles are released and brushed away.",
