                        "mode_of_action": "1. A nanoscopic coating is applied to fabric fibers, creating a structured surface with very low surface energy. 2. When liquids or dirt come into contact, they are unable to wet the surface and bead up. 3. Contaminants can be easily removed by shaking, brushing, or a light rinse, without penetrating the fabric.",
