                        "mode_of_action": "1. Dormant microbes (e.g., spores) are embedded in fibers during manufacturing. 2. Ambient moisture or body humidity activates the microbes. 3. The microbes consume sweat, oils, and organic soil as nutrients. 4. The fabric remains hygienically clean for extended periods, requiring only occasional, minimal-water rinsing.",
