                        "idea_summary": "A fabric designed for on-demand hygiene by releasing a payload of sanitizing agents (e.g., nitric oxide, natural antimicrobials) directly in response to sweat. This provides a proactive, targeted sanitization effect, differentiating it from methods that break down existing soil.",
                        "core_principle": "Encapsulates chemical sanitizing agents within the fabric matrix, which are released upon rupture or increased permeability of the capsules triggered by moisture.",
                        "form_factor": "A conventional-feeling textile containing microcapsules that release a payload when activated by sweat.",
                        "mode_of_action": "1. Microcapsules containing a sanitizing agent are embedded in the fabric. 2. Moisture from sweat causes the microcapsule shells to swell, rupture, or become permeable. 3. The sanitizing agent is released in a controlled dose, neutralizing odor-causing bacteria and pathogens. 4. The effect is localized to damp areas of the garment.",
