                        "mode_of_action": "1. Engineered microbes are integrated into the fabric. 2. When activated by moisture, the microbes establish a biofilm. 3. Upon sensing specific soil molecules, the microbes upregulate production of targeted enzymes (e.g., lipases for oils, proteases for proteins) or biosurfactants. 4. The secreted agents break down stains locally, requiring no external detergents.",
