                        "form_factor": "A fabric treatment or finish containing dormant, soil-responsive microorganisms.",
                        "mode_of_action": "1. Dormant microbes are thinly and evenly applied to the fabric as a finish. 2. A spill or stain occurs, providing a sudden source of nutrients and moisture. 3. The microbes in direct contact with the soil activate and begin to rapidly multiply, forming a visible or invisible 'hotspot' of intense enzymatic activity. 4. Once the soil is consumed, the microbes return to a dormant state.",
