                "name": "Ideas that mimic natural biological processes or materials for cleaning",
                "description": "Solutions that draw inspiration from or directly copy mechanisms, structures (e.g., for filtration, surface architectures for antimicrobial effects or foul-release, abiotic barrier mimicry, secretory glands, carnivorous plant strategies, protein-based interactions), or processes found in nature (biomimicry) to achieve cleaning, repellency, or hygiene on textiles. This can include adapting principles into non-living systems, using desiccation-induced changes, or adapting extracellular digestion.",
