                        "mode_of_action": "1. Dormant, beneficial microbes (e.g., spores) are embedded into the fabric fibers during manufacturing. 2. Ambient humidity or a light mist hydrates the fibers, activating the microbial consortium. 3. The microbes metabolize organic soil and odor-causing compounds as a food source. 4. The fabric remains hygienically clean for extended periods, requiring only occasional light misting for reactivation.",
