                        "optimized_idea": "Textiles with Triggered-Release Microcapsules of Cleaning Bio-Agents",
                        "idea_summary": "A smart textile embedded with microcapsules containing dormant cleaning agents (microbes or enzymes). These capsules rupture or become permeable in response to moisture or specific chemical triggers from soiling, releasing a concentrated dose of cleaning power precisely where and when it's needed.",
                        "core_principle": "Microencapsulation technology protects dormant microbes or enzymes within the fabric structure, ensuring their stability and enabling triggered release upon specific conditions.",
                        "form_factor": "Textiles containing microscopic capsules integrated into or coated onto the fibers. The capsules contain dormant microbes, spores, or stabilized enzymes.",
                        "mode_of_action": "1. Microcapsules containing dormant microbes or enzymes are embedded into fabric fibers. 2. The protective shell shields the active agents from degradation. 3. Contact with moisture (sweat, mist) or a specific soil compound triggers the capsule to release its contents. 4. The released agents break down the local soil and odor, achieving targeted cleaning.",
