                        "idea_summary": "A 'rechargeable' antimicrobial fabric that maintains a hygienic surface by slowly releasing protective agents or having its properties reactivated by a minimal input like light or mist. This approach extends the time between washes by providing a persistent, low-level defense against microbial growth.",
                        "core_principle": "Embeds encapsulated antimicrobial or odor-neutralizing agents into textile fibers that are released slowly over time or when triggered by a specific stimulus like moisture.",
                        "form_factor": "A textile material containing microcapsules of active ingredients like natural biocides, pH-adjusting compounds, or odor-trapping molecules.",
