                        "optimized_idea": "Compact Home Bioreactor for Laundry Greywater Recycling",
                        "idea_summary": "A compact, in-home bioreactor that captures, purifies, and recycles laundry greywater using a highly efficient biofilm. This closed-loop system dramatically reduces a household's net water consumption for laundry by treating and reusing the water from each wash cycle.",
                        "core_principle": "Leverages a permanent, cultivated biofilm on a contained, reusable appliance surface to purify laundry greywater for immediate reuse.",
                        "form_factor": "A compact, modular bioreactor unit designed to integrate with a washing machine's water outlet/inlet.",
                        "mode_of_action": "1. Greywater from a wash cycle is diverted into the bioreactor unit. 2. The water passes through media (e.g., porous ceramics, textiles) hosting a robust cleaning biofilm. 3. The biofilm metabolizes detergents, soils, and microbes from the water. 4. The purified water is stored in a reservoir, ready for the next wash cycle.",
