                        "form_factor": "A textile finish or grafted molecule that is permanently bonded to the fabric fibers, providing a persistent, non-living catalytic activity.",
                        "mode_of_action": "1. Stabilized enzymes (e.g., lipases, proteases) are chemically grafted onto textile fibers during manufacturing. 2. The garment is worn. 3. Minimal moisture (humidity, light mist) activates the immobilized enzymes. 4. The enzymes catalytically decompose specific organic soils they come into contact with.",
