                        "idea_summary": "This concept involves a fabric coating that is not only dirt-repellent and antimicrobial but can also autonomously repair minor damage, ensuring its high performance is maintained over time. This synergy between repellency and durability provides long-lasting hygiene and reduces the need for washing far more effectively than a standard coating.",
                        "core_principle": "A multi-layered polymer coating combines a superhydrophobic, antibacterial outer surface with an underlying self-healing matrix that flows to repair minor scratches or abrasions.",
                        "form_factor": "A durable, multi-functional coating applied to standard textiles.",
                        "mode_of_action": "1. The superhydrophobic outer layer repels water, soil, and microbes. 2. When this layer is scratched, the underlying self-healing polymer flows into the gap, restoring the surface integrity. 3. This ensures the antibacterial and repellent properties remain effective throughout the garment's lifecycle.",
