                        "mode_of_action": "1. Engineered spores (e.g., *B. subtilis*) are integrated into fabric fibers. 2. The spores remain inert until activated by moisture. 3. Upon activation, the microbes express pre-programmed genes to produce and secrete cleaning compounds (e.g., lipase enzymes for oil stains). 4. The agents act locally to break down soil, after which the microbes may return to a dormant state.",
