                        "mode_of_action": "1. Dormant, safe microbes (e.g., spores) are embedded into fabric fibers during manufacturing. 2. Ambient humidity or a light mist activates the microbes. 3. The microbes consume organic soil (sweat, skin cells) as nutrients, breaking them down. 4. The fabric remains hygienically clean, drastically reducing the need for water-intensive washing.",
