                        "optimized_idea": "Stimulus-Activated Antimicrobial Release",
                        "idea_summary": "A 'smart' textile that keeps its antimicrobial agents in reserve, releasing them only when and where they are needed. By responding to triggers like the pH change from sweat or the presence of moisture, this system provides highly targeted, on-demand hygiene while conserving its protective power for when it matters most.",
                        "core_principle": "Encapsulates potent antimicrobial agents within a smart polymer matrix that is designed to release its payload only when triggered by a specific environmental cue.",
                        "form_factor": "A fabric finish or fiber additive containing micro-encapsulated antimicrobial agents.",
                        "mode_of_action": "1. Antimicrobial agents are sealed within microscopic capsules integrated into the fabric. 2. The capsule walls are designed to break down in response to a specific trigger (e.g., pH < 6.0, high humidity). 3. When the trigger occurs (e.g., a person sweats), the capsules rupture and release their antimicrobial payload. 4. The local area is sanitized, preventing microbial growth.",
