                        "idea_summary": "A high-tech cleaning spray that uses bio-derived nanoparticles (OMVs) to deliver enzymes for stain removal. This approach mimics natural intercellular transport to create a highly effective, targeted, and stable delivery system for next-generation biological cleaners.",
                        "core_principle": "Leverages bio-engineered Outer Membrane Vesicles (OMVs) as natural nanocarriers to deliver a highly concentrated and protected payload of cleaning enzymes directly to stains.",
                        "form_factor": "A liquid formulation in a spray bottle, containing a high concentration of enzyme-loaded OMVs.",
                        "mode_of_action": "1. Bacteria are genetically engineered to overproduce specific cleaning enzymes and package them into their outer membrane vesicles. 2. These enzyme-loaded OMVs are harvested, purified, and formulated into an aqueous spray. 3. When sprayed on a stain, the vesicles adhere to the fabric and soil, delivering their concentrated enzyme payload directly where it's needed. 4. The vesicle structure protects the enzymes, increasing their stability and efficacy.",
