                        "core_principle": "The fabric incorporates materials with high specific surface area and specific chemical affinities (e.g., activated carbon, zeolites) to physically adsorb odor molecules and organic compounds.",
                        "form_factor": "Clothing made from composite fibers containing micro-particles of an adsorbent material. The garment is 'cleaned' by a process that regenerates the adsorbent material.",
                        "mode_of_action": "1. During wear, volatile organic compounds (odors) and other contaminants are trapped by the adsorbent material within the fibers. 2. The garment feels and smells fresh for longer. 3. To clean, the garment is placed in a special unit that applies low heat or a vacuum. 4. The trapped compounds are released from the adsorbent and vented, regenerating the fabric for the next wear.",
